      <levelledPara>
        <title>Structural and Content Model Rules BREX</title>
        <para>
          This BREX defines structural and content model validation rules for ATA 31 
          (Indicating/Recording) AMM data modules. It enforces proper use of S1000D 
          structural elements and content modeling conventions.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Mandatory Structural Elements</title>
        <para>
          All ATA 31 AMM data modules must use the following structural elements 
          appropriately:
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;descr&gt; for descriptive content
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;proceduralStep&gt; for step-by-step procedures
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;warning&gt; for safety warnings
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;caution&gt; for equipment protection notices
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;note&gt; for supplementary information
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Content Separation Rules</title>
        <para>
          Rule 1: No Mixed Procedural/Descriptive Logic
        </para>
        <para>
          Descriptive and procedural content must be in separate data modules.
          A single DM cannot contain both description and procedures.
        </para>
        <para>
          Rule 2: One Primary Task Per Procedural DM
        </para>
        <para>
          Each procedural data module must focus on a single primary maintenance task
          (e.g., "Remove Flight Data Recorder" or "Test Cockpit Voice Recorder").
        </para>
        <para>
          Rule 3: No Embedded Publication Module Logic
        </para>
        <para>
          Data modules must not contain PM-level logic such as TOC generation,
          cross-references to other publications, or publication-specific formatting.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Procedural Step Requirements</title>
        <para>
          Each procedural step must:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Have a clear action verb (e.g., "Remove", "Install", "Test", "Inspect")
        </para>
        <para>
          - Include necessary conditions and prerequisites
        </para>
        <para>
          - Specify required tools and materials
        </para>
        <para>
          - Include verification steps where applicable
        </para>
        <para>
          - Be numbered sequentially within the procedure
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Warning and Caution Placement</title>
        <para>
          Warnings and cautions must:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Be placed BEFORE the step they apply to
        </para>
        <para>
          - Use standard AMPEL360 warning/caution templates
        </para>
        <para>
          - Reference specific hazards or risks
        </para>
        <para>
          - Include mitigation actions
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Content Reuse and Common Information</title>
        <para>
          Rule: Use Common Information Repositories
        </para>
        <para>
          Frequently used warnings, cautions, and standard procedures must be
          defined in the COMMON directory and referenced via &lt;dmRef&gt; or
          entity references, not duplicated in each DM.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Cross-Reference Rules</title>
        <para>
          Internal references within ATA 31 must use:
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;dmRef&gt; for references to other data modules
        </para>
        <para>
          - &lt;internalRef&gt; for references within the same DM
        </para>
        <para>
          - Proper applicability statements for conditional references
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Metadata Requirements</title>
        <para>
          All data modules must include:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Complete identAndStatusSection
        </para>
        <para>
          - Proper security classification
        </para>
        <para>
          - Responsible partner company identification
        </para>
        <para>
          - Applicability statement (even if "All")
        </para>
        <para>
          - Quality assurance status
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Prohibited Constructs</title>
        <para>
          The following structural patterns are prohibited:
        </para>
        <para>
          - Empty levelledPara elements
        </para>
        <para>
          - Procedural steps without action verbs
        </para>
        <para>
          - Warnings/cautions placed after the hazardous step
        </para>
        <para>
          - Multiple unrelated procedures in a single DM
        </para>
        <para>
          - Inline graphics without proper ICN references
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
